<div id="TcHmiTextblock_654" data-tchmi-type="TcHmi.Controls.Beckhoff.TcHmiTextblock" data-tchmi-height="292" data-tchmi-height-unit="px" data-tchmi-left="335" data-tchmi-left-unit="px" data-tchmi-text="The EK1100 EtherCAT Coupler is the link between the EtherCAT protocol at fieldbus level and the EtherCAT Terminals.\n\nThe coupler converts the passing telegrams from Ethernet 100BASE-TX to E-bus signal representation.\n\nThe EK1100 has two RJ45 sockets. The upper Ethernet interface is used to connect the coupler to the network; the lower socket serves for the optional connection of further EtherCAT devices in the same segment." data-tchmi-top="183" data-tchmi-top-unit="px" data-tchmi-width="611" data-tchmi-width-unit="px" data-tchmi-word-wrap="True" data-tchmi-text-font-size="20" data-tchmi-zindex="1">
</div>
